# Site UFM / Topaz Availability

Not every site has a UFM instance we can reach. Before running `ufm-cli`,
`ufm_*` MCP tools, or `topaz-*` commands, confirm the site is accessible below.

If a site is listed as **no access**, do **not** attempt those tools — tell the
user immediately that fabric monitoring is unavailable for that site.

## Site Matrix

| Site | UFM site key | Topaz AZ ID | Notes |
|------|-------------|-------------|-------|
| ORI-TX | `ori` | `us-south-2a` | |
| APLD-2 (pod 3) | `apld2` | `us-central-4a` | Elevenlabs, Rockyraven clusters |
| APLD-2 (pod 2) | `apld2_p2` | `us-central-4b` | |
| 5C-OH1 | `5c_oh1` | `us-central-8a` | |
| 5C-MD1 | `5c_md1` | `us-east-3a` | |
| 5C-TN1 | `5c_tn1` | `us-south-3a` | |
| IREN-H200 | supported | `ca-west-1a` | |
| IREN-B300-1 | **no access** | `ca-west-1c` | UFM managed by IREN — Topaz access via ca-west-1c |

## What To Do When a Site Has No Access

1. Stop — do not try `ufm-cli`, `ufm_*` MCP, or `topaz-*` commands.
2. Tell the user: "UFM/Topaz is not accessible for this site."
3. For IREN-B300-1 specifically, UFM is not accessible but Topaz is
   available via `ca-west-1c`. For full fabric diagnostics, work with
   IREN support or use ibdiagnet data collected on-box.
